  <section class="about-body shell">
    <p class="section-index">Practice</p>
    <div class="about-prose">
      <p>My background spans autonomous and interactive systems, multimodal tracking and reasoning, long-context architectures, distributed model training, GPU kernels, and low-latency inference infrastructure. Across those settings, the recurring problem is the same: make a model’s behaviour measurable, then build enough of the stack to test the explanation.</p>
      <p>My current public direction centres on reinforcement learning and alignment for embodied AI—particularly the relationship between representations, latent world-action models, policies, and the feedback used to shape them.</p>
      <p>I completed graduate research at IIT Kanpur on efficient and robust discriminative manifold learning and multi-modal multi-object tracking. Public technical writing and code are linked from this site; employer-confidential work is intentionally not described here.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

